Chapter: ProofSmoke

 End-to-end smoke test for the propositional-equality proof layer:
 reflexivity, symmetry, transitivity, and congruence. Each proof is a
 definition whose declared type is a propositional equality; the
 checker verifies the body against that type and the emitter erases it
 (CDX4020), so the program's only runtime output is the confirmation
 line. Successful compilation is the real assertion.

 These use the plain annotated-definition form, which the type checker
 verifies. The claim/proof/qed sugar is parsed but its claim type is
 not yet threaded to the proof body, so it is exercised separately as a
 skipped test.

Section: Reflexivity

  refl-int : Integer === Integer
  refl-int = Refl

Section: Symmetry

  sym-int : Integer === Integer
  sym-int = sym Refl

Section: Transitivity

  trans-int : Integer === Integer
  trans-int = trans Refl Refl

Section: Congruence

 From a proof that a === b, cong derives f a === f b. Here Refl proves
 Integer === Integer, and cong lifts it under the List constructor.

  cong-list : (List Integer) === (List Integer)
  cong-list = cong Refl

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "proofs ok"
  end
